## [SPEC-FIXTURE]
## Category: Invalid
## Feature: Ownership Move Semantics (Use After Move)
## Spec Reference: docs/language-spec/ownership-and-memory.md#2-value-semantics-copy-vs-move
## Violation: Variable 'original_data' was moved into 'transferred_data' and subsequently referenced.
## Expected Diagnostic: WON-MEM-001: Use of moved value 'original_data'. Value was moved to 'transferred_data' on line 12.

struct DynamicPayload:
    content: str

fn process(payload: DynamicPayload):
    println("Content: {payload.content}")

fn main():
    let original_data = DynamicPayload { content: "Critical Data" }
    let transferred_data = original_data    # Ownership moved here

    process(original_data)                  # Reject: original_data is invalidated
